#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
p10bare.py - small PDP-6/KA10/KI10/KS10/KL10 SIMH bare-metal test runner.

Current design:
  * machines: pdp6, ka10, ki10 (ks10/kl10 support is limited)
  * Uses the system PDP-10 cross toolchain when available:
      - pdp10-dec-none-gcc (driver) for C -> assembly
      - pdp10-dec-none-as     DAS-compatible assembler (respects PDP10_AS)
      - dxrconvert            for SIMH/RIM image conversion
  * Supports pdp6, ka10, ki10, ks10, kl10 machines.
  * PDP10_PREFIX is required and is the default root for the compiler,
    assembler, mkrim, and SIMH tools.
  * Tool lookup uses explicit environment overrides first.
  * Emulator paths can be overridden via SIMH_PDP6, SIMH_KA, SIMH_KI, etc.
  * INI files are searched in workdir, toolsdir, and the installed data directory
  * default workdir is the current directory
  * default execution image mode is RIM; deposit mode remains available
  * default ini lookup: workdir first, then the directory containing p10bare.py
  * no dependency on simh_baretest.py

Artifacts per run:
  NAME.rim
  NAME.simh
  NAME-run.ini
  NAME.out
  NAME.labels
  NAME.report.txt
"""

